WEBVTT

00:00:03.316 --> 00:00:05.057
- don't believe it.
- Don't you?

00:00:05.231 --> 00:00:06.493
- It's impossible.
- Is it?

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:07.581
- It couldn't be.
- Couldn't it?

00:00:07.755 --> 00:00:08.539
I'm--Are you?

00:00:08.713 --> 00:00:09.888
Imposter!

00:00:10.062 --> 00:00:12.325
You stole my babies!

00:00:12.499 --> 00:00:15.676
But they know
who their real daddy is...

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:16.938
drone-napper!

00:00:17.112 --> 00:00:18.636
[chortling]

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.900
Magnificent creations,
my boy.

00:00:22.074 --> 00:00:24.642
I borrowed them
to lure you here

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:26.818
and reunite our family.

00:00:28.559 --> 00:00:30.213
You see, Ivo...

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:35.348
I'm your grandfather:

00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:37.959
Gerald Robotnik.

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:44.705
My... grandfather?

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.319
But how? And why?

00:00:50.102 --> 00:00:52.147
And who did what with whom?

00:00:52.322 --> 00:00:57.240
You hail from an ancestry
of excellence...

00:00:57.414 --> 00:00:59.981
tied directly <i>à moi.</i>

00:01:00.155 --> 00:01:03.071
Yes, I know French.

00:01:05.596 --> 00:01:07.119
You do look like me.

00:01:08.076 --> 00:01:10.035
But fatter. And older.

00:01:10.905 --> 00:01:12.864
And there's that funny smell.

00:01:14.561 --> 00:01:17.390
But the resemblance
is uncanny.

00:01:18.261 --> 00:01:19.871
It's as if...

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:22.134
[both]
...we're two characters
in a movie

00:01:22.308 --> 00:01:24.876
being played
by the same actor.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.487
- But I need real proof!
- Ivo!

00:01:27.661 --> 00:01:28.967
We have very little time.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.623
But I could field
a couple of queries.

00:01:32.797 --> 00:01:35.930
Name the most elegant formula
in mathematics.

00:01:36.104 --> 00:01:37.454
Euler's Identity.

00:01:37.628 --> 00:01:39.934
E to the I times pi plus one
equals zilch.

00:01:40.108 --> 00:01:41.936
European capitals
arranged alphabetically

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.373
by the fourth letter.

00:01:43.547 --> 00:01:45.288
Riga, Monaco, Sarajevo, Tirana.

00:01:45.462 --> 00:01:47.246
The speed of light
divided by
the speed of sound,

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.466
divided by
the speed of the bus
in the movie <i>Speed.</i>

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.989
[mimics adding machine]

00:01:51.163 --> 00:01:53.731
17,893.33333...

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:57.343
Rounding up?17,894 MPH.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.998
And, for all the marbles...

00:02:00.172 --> 00:02:02.348
Good. I lost mine.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.568
A rare lung disease,

00:02:04.742 --> 00:02:07.832
and the longest word
in the English dictionary.

00:02:08.485 --> 00:02:09.964
Um...

00:02:10.138 --> 00:02:13.446
[both] Pneumonoultramicroscopic-
silicovolcanoconiosis!

00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:17.972
- Pap-pap!
- In the saggy flesh.

00:02:18.146 --> 00:02:20.235
But looking pretty good
for a hundred and ten.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.976
[shuddering grunt]

00:02:22.673 --> 00:02:25.284
Oh, Grampy-poo! [laughs]

00:02:28.679 --> 00:02:32.465
Where have you been
my entire life?

00:02:32.639 --> 00:02:34.206
[moans happily]

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.382
[gasps] Wait.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.776
Where have you been...
my entire life?

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:44.956
Locked in
a top-secret prison
for the last 50 years.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.394
Made it kind of hard
to send Christmas cards.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.048
Now...

00:02:50.222 --> 00:02:53.791
you're probably wondering
why I brought you here.

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.358
You didn't bring me here!

00:02:55.532 --> 00:02:58.839
I used my unparalleled intellect
to track you down.

00:02:59.013 --> 00:03:02.930
Per the plan
I concocted with
my unparalleled intellect.

00:03:03.104 --> 00:03:04.889
You'll see.

00:03:05.063 --> 00:03:07.631
I have the answer
to everything.

00:03:09.241 --> 00:03:10.895
Come on, kiddo.

00:03:19.294 --> 00:03:21.688
[groaning]

00:03:24.691 --> 00:03:26.650
Oh, no. Oh, no, no.

00:03:26.824 --> 00:03:28.652
Someone tell me
this is some kind of

00:03:28.826 --> 00:03:30.958
concussion-induced nightmare.

00:03:31.132 --> 00:03:33.265
There's two Eggmen now?

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:35.441
Double your villains,
double your fun!

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:38.401
Two Robotniks
are way worse than one.

00:03:38.575 --> 00:03:39.576
Chest bump?

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:40.577
No.

00:03:41.665 --> 00:03:43.754
Stone,
why are you tied up?

00:03:43.928 --> 00:03:46.496
Do that on your own time.
You sicken me.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.063
You must be
the long-lost grandson.

00:03:49.237 --> 00:03:52.110
And you must be
another stinking hedgehog.

00:03:52.284 --> 00:03:54.329
So you're the one
behind all this.

00:03:54.504 --> 00:03:56.723
- The Shadow breakout.
- The attack on Walters.

00:03:56.897 --> 00:03:58.072
That musty
old-man smell.

00:03:58.246 --> 00:04:00.205
How dare you insult me

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:02.033
with your unsolicited
exposition!

00:04:02.207 --> 00:04:04.296
Shadow, get the key.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.471
Where is it?

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:07.734
Ha! Good one, Hot Topic.

00:04:07.908 --> 00:04:09.997
Do you really think
we'd be that stupid

00:04:10.171 --> 00:04:12.217
to bring the key
right to you?

00:04:12.391 --> 00:04:13.827
Yep, we're that stupid.

00:04:14.001 --> 00:04:16.177
GUN took everything from us.

00:04:16.351 --> 00:04:19.267
And now we are going
to take everything from them.

00:04:19.442 --> 00:04:20.704
[Gerald] With this.

00:04:20.878 --> 00:04:24.534
My masterpiece
of malevolence...

00:04:24.708 --> 00:04:27.232
The Eclipse Cannon.

00:04:27.406 --> 00:04:30.496
<i>In exchange
for my freedom,</i>

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.803
<i>I gave GUN
the most powerful weapon</i>

00:04:32.977 --> 00:04:35.501
<i>mankind has ever seen,</i>

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:38.243
<i>capable of delivering
a precision strike</i>

00:04:38.417 --> 00:04:39.810
<i>anywhere on Earth.</i>

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:42.465
<i>Our first target:</i>

00:04:43.291 --> 00:04:44.945
<i>GUN Headquarters.</i>

00:04:45.119 --> 00:04:47.252
But firing a weapon
that powerful

00:04:47.426 --> 00:04:49.384
could threaten millions
of innocent lives!

00:04:49.559 --> 00:04:51.822
Yeah, tera-bite me.[cackles]

00:04:51.996 --> 00:04:56.870
This is one of two keys required
to launch the Eclipse Cannon.

00:04:57.044 --> 00:04:59.351
The other is locked
inside GUN headquarters.

00:04:59.525 --> 00:05:01.396
Once we have both,

00:05:01.571 --> 00:05:04.399
I will take rightful control
of my weapon.

00:05:04.574 --> 00:05:06.358
I'm in.

00:05:13.321 --> 00:05:14.801
Holy crab!

00:05:14.975 --> 00:05:16.586
[Robotnik]
Spacious and crustaceous.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.675
Thank you so much

00:05:18.849 --> 00:05:20.503
for inspiring
this little adventure.

00:05:20.677 --> 00:05:22.853
It really worked out
for me.

00:05:23.027 --> 00:05:25.986
And you wonder why
I have trust issues!

00:05:27.466 --> 00:05:29.642
Shadow, wait! Don't do this.

00:05:29.816 --> 00:05:31.209
I know you're hurting,

00:05:31.383 --> 00:05:33.907
but don't let that change
who you are inside.

00:05:34.081 --> 00:05:38.346
I've spent 50 years
reliving what they did to her.

00:05:38.521 --> 00:05:41.436
This is who I am inside.

